IMPORT prelude

-- Workers' Compensation (Dust Diseases) Act 1942 (NSW) -- the dates, in one small module. It uses only the built-in
-- date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), FLOOR and MODULO, not
-- the daydate library, and defines no YMD.
--
-- READINGS (forks in NOTES.md):
-- F7  "within 2 working days after" (s 8(1A)): the second Monday-to-Friday day after the later trigger day; public
--     holidays are not skipped, because no list of them is deposited.
-- F8  "within 6 months after" (s 8I(1A)): ends on the same day of the month six months later, or that month's last day
--     where the month is shorter.
-- F9  "attained the age of 16 years" (s 8(2B)(ba)): on the 16th anniversary of birth; a 29 February birthday is
--     reached on 1 March in a common year.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website at 10 March 2025, via the Open Australian
-- Legal Corpus (version as at 18 October 2022). State of New South Wales, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE
-- ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Workers' Compensation (Dust Diseases) Act 1942`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the first day` `to` `the second day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the second day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the first day`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus days` n MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS n)

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `the first day` `and` `the second day` MEANS
    IF `the first day` `is before` `the second day` THEN `the second day` ELSE `the first day`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` a `and` b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` a `and` b MEANS IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- Fork F8: the same day of the month n months later, or that month's last day where it is shorter.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus months` n MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (`the smaller of` (DATE_DAY `the day`) `and` (`the number of days in month` `the new month` `of` `the new year`)) `the new month` `the new year`
    WHERE
        `the month count` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the day` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the new year`    MEANS FLOOR (`the month count` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the new month`   MEANS (`the month count` MINUS (`the new year` TIMES 12)) PLUS 1

-- Day of the week from the serial: 9 November 2026 (a Monday) has a serial that leaves 1 on division by 7, so
-- 1 = Monday ... 5 = Friday, 6 = Saturday, 0 = Sunday.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a working day` `the day` IF
    (DATE_SERIAL `the day` MODULO 7) AT LEAST 1 AND (DATE_SERIAL `the day` MODULO 7) AT MOST 5

-- Fork F7: the n-th working day after a day (the day itself not counted).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the working day` n `after` `the day` MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN `the day`
    ELSE IF `is a working day` `the next day`
         THEN `the working day` (n MINUS 1) `after` `the next day`
         ELSE `the working day` n `after` `the next day`
    WHERE
        `the next day` MEANS `the day` `plus days` 1

-- Fork F9: the age in whole years on a day.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `the day of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the age on` `the day` `of someone born on` `the day of birth` MEANS
    IF    (DATE_MONTH `the day` LESS THAN DATE_MONTH `the day of birth`)
       OR (    DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS DATE_MONTH `the day of birth`
           AND DATE_DAY `the day` LESS THAN DATE_DAY `the day of birth`)
    THEN `the year difference` MINUS 1
    ELSE `the year difference`
    WHERE
        `the year difference` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the day` MINUS DATE_YEAR `the day of birth`
